				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/juicenotjava" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7084554); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7084554&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607435981" alt="JuiceNotJava" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7084554)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/juicenotjava" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7084554); return false;" >JuiceNotJava</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607435610 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Dec 2020 13:53</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50863/general">General Discussion / General</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-2134523/what-is-your-favourite-scp">What is your favourite SCP?</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839731">
									

<p>There are a ton of SCPs I've read, and I can't really choose a favorite out the ones I truly enjoyed but nevertheless, here are my favorites:</p>
<p>SCP-4205 for format-screw. Having the computer terminal display the articles and the start-up really tickled my aesthetic taste. The story of the SCP itself is not bad either, and I thoroughly enjoyed it.</p>
<p>SCP-5000 for story. The realization that hits you after digging deep terrifies the ever living crap out of me. Coupled with the fact that I believe in my own humanity, this SCP really brings chill down my spine and, quite frankly, I enjoy it.</p>
<p>SCP-001-EX for the proposal. Good boys are good, bad boys are bad. Is there anything left to say other than I liked this proposal more than the Ouroboros Cycle? Perhaps not.</p>
<p>Lastly, SCP-914. The experiment logs are the articles I most often come back to simply because it's a lot easier to digest.</p>

