<p>Seeking Greenlights: yes.</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Other (Just an informative article)</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): The draft I made is at the bottom.</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: There is a dice that if you come within a certain range of it rolls itself and on a 6 you die, on a 1 you live and a two to five you suffer increasing server injuries.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: There is this dice of unknown origin that seems to have the power to randomly kill anything that comes near it however changes of death is random and sometimes they are unharmed or barley harmed. (You can see the draft I made at the bottom of this page).</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: Now I'm going to be very honest here, I didn't think about what would make it stand out. But I mean I suppose it's unique because it could be easily used to kill even the most powerful SCPs as long as those SCPs are alive however the chances of it doing nothing or barely anything is too high to actually test the theory.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: It's my first SCP ever so there is probably a lot of points anyone could comment on but I suppose my main concern is whether it is formal enough.</p>
