<p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> [All information regarding SCP-5170 is to be hidden from level 1 personnel or less if a person of such level accesses information regarding SCP-5170 they are to immediately receive Class-B Amnestics. SCP-5232 is to be kept in a 30m<sup>2</sup> cell and protocol 202-5232-A</p>
<p>Protocol 202-5232-A forbids any foundation personnel to enter the cell unless they have already come within 30m of this SCP before the protocol was in place, tests with D-CLASS on SCP-5232 is still allowed as long as as the test is done by a level 3 or higher researcher.</p>
<p>Any cleaning of SCP-5232's cell is to be done by a D-CLASS janitor or any janitor who has come in contact with SCP-5232 beforehand and survived.</p>
<p>It has also been concluded impossible to destroy SCP-5232 and impossible to stop it rolling.</p>
<p><strong>Description:</strong> [SCP-5232 is a six-sided silver dice of unknown origin. SCP-5232 does not show any anomalies properties until an entity (human, animal, plant and SCP all included) comes within 30m<sup>2</sup> of the SCP, if an entity comes within 30m<sup>2</sup> the dice will then proceed to roll itself, which tests have shown is completely randomized.</p>
<p>Once it has done this, if the higher value the number value displayed on the top of the dice, the higher level of damage the entity suffers. Tests show there is no way to cancel the anomalous effects and tests show the type of damage/death the entity suffers is also randomized. Also, a roll of one so far appears to guarantee no damage and a roll of six so far appears to guarantee instant death.]</p>
