<p>&#8230;<br />
So it’s just scp 682 but a spider&#8230;? Honestly I would recommend dropping the idea.</p>
<p>But if you insist to make this a good scp idea, then here’s some advice:</p>
<h2><span>You <strong>need</strong> some kind of story.</span></h2>
<p>Currently you only have an object, but that’s it an object. We don’t know where it was found, why is it deadly. An easy way to improve this scp would be adding ,let’s say&#8230; exploration logs! Exploration logs are an easy way to make an scp engaging and helps to create some deep lore in a creative way.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A huge spider that is quite venomous and difficult to contain.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That’s half of the SCPs out there for ya. You need a more unique hook.</p>
<p>Anyway good luck with your skip! ^-^</p>

