<p>How do you do. I'm Piecemaker and I am honored to at last find myself in the Foundation.</p>
<p>I've been reading through various documentation for years with many favorites to speak of, and have recently decided it might be time for me to write one of my own. I'm gathered numerous experiences over the years through games, books, movies and I've always had a thing for creepy or unsettling things, which is why I often recommend SCP to my colleagues and friends.</p>
<p>That being said, I wish for my first document to be on a humanoid SCP. I have a rather specific concept in mind that I've been going over in my head for <em>weeks</em>. Now, I know, it's not recommended to start with a humanoid. How do I know? Because I've read through every guide I could get my hands on, from &quot;So you wanna write a humanoid&quot; to &quot;Things what do a thing&quot;, as well as going through some 50 crits in the Ideas critique forum to see common pitfalls. I am nevertheless <em>terrified</em> of falling into an X-man syndrome or another common mistake, as the concept is rather close to me. Either way, I intend to give it my very best effort. See you in the Crit Forum.</p>

