<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong></p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A used car lot in Colorado that offers dirt-cheap classic autos. All owners crash fatally after a week of driving.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The Foundation notices an absurdly sharp increase in automotive-related deaths tracing back to a single car lot and, after some investigating, designate it an anomaly, including all staff. Interview logs with staff members. Surveilance instated in a garage which seemingly provides the lot with its cars - proved futile as when a car appears, recording equipment malfunctions and witnesses black out.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Final Destination-style elaborate death setups.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Crashes aim to also kill bystanders. <em>Spectacularly.</em> Hence the death toll.</p>

